## Python Instruction
Write a python function to check if a given string is a valid URL or not. A valid URL should start with 'http://' or 'https://', followed by a domain name, and can have optional path, query string, or fragment identifier.

## Python Solution
```python
import re

def isValidUrl(url):
    regex = r'^(http|https)://[a-zA-Z0-9-]+(\.[a-zA-Z0-9-]+)+(/[a-zA-Z0-9.,@:%_\+~#?&//=]*)?$'
    if re.match(regex, url):
        return True
    else:
        return False
```

## Python Tests
assert isValidUrl('http://www.example.com') == True
assert isValidUrl('ftp://www.example.com') == False
assert isValidUrl('https://www.example.com/path?query=string#fragment') == True
assert isValidUrl('http://www.example.com/path') == True
assert isValidUrl('http://') == False
assert isValidUrl('www.example.com') == False

## Canonical Elixir names (use verbatim)
- Module: `Solution`
- Function: `isvalidurl`

